  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.97,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted curve rises suddenly to a flat ~0.93–0.99 plateau from 8 h onward. That could mean real stationary phase or a reader that saturates, so I checked whether the reader responds proportionally. I diluted the retained aliquots and multiplied the readings back up. At 18 h, a 10x dilution read 0.0991 and 0.0972, which corrects to ~0.98. A 4x dilution read 0.2449 and 0.2332, which corrects to ~0.96. Both match the undiluted reading of 0.964, and the two dilutions agree with each other. If the reader were saturating, the corrected values would be well above the undiluted reading and would get bigger as dilution increased. At 14 h, a 10x dilution read 0.0974 and 0.0980, which corrects to ~0.98. That is close to the undiluted 0.931 and within the ~0.93–0.99 scatter of the plateau readings. The reader is therefore linear up to about 1.0, and the plateau is real stationary-phase biomass. Late biomass is at the level the undiluted readings show, about 0.96–0.98 at 18 h. Limitation: the earlier plateau points (8–13 h, 15–17 h) were not tested directly. This conclusion rests on the 14 h and 18 h checks."
  },
